to the biggest party

257
00:10:55.524 --> 00:10:56.786
the world has ever seen."

258
00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.919
-Queen of Rock?
-KING PEPPY: It's nothing!

259
00:10:58.962 --> 00:11:01.704
It means nothing at all.
It's just junk mail.

260
00:11:01.748 --> 00:11:02.879
You don't need
to worry about it.

261
00:11:02.923 --> 00:11:04.185
I mean, quit looking at it,
everyone.

262
00:11:04.228 --> 00:11:05.839
Forget what you saw!

263
00:11:05.882 --> 00:11:07.101
[chewing noisily]

264
00:11:07.144 --> 00:11:08.189
[Branch yells]

265
00:11:08.232 --> 00:11:10.060
-[grunting]
-[shushing]

266
00:11:10.104 --> 00:11:11.714
-There you go. There you go.
-[eyes boinging]

267
00:11:11.758 --> 00:11:14.108
-Calm down. Calm down.
-[purring]

268
00:11:14.151 --> 00:11:15.849
[quietly]:
There you go.

269
00:11:16.893 --> 00:11:19.113
Okay, I'm calm.

270
00:11:19.156 --> 00:11:20.114
I'm calm.

271
00:11:20.157 --> 00:11:22.333
Dad, what's going on?

272
00:11:22.377 --> 00:11:25.641
Well, I have long feared
this day would come.

273
00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:28.775
I was hoping to protect you
from this, Poppy.

274
00:11:28.818 --> 00:11:29.863
Protect me?

275
00:11:29.906 --> 00:11:31.255
I'm not a little kid
anymore, Dad.

276
00:11:31.299 --> 00:11:32.648
I'm the queen now.

277
00:11:33.475 --> 00:11:35.782
You're right.

278
00:11:35.825 --> 00:11:40.787
The truth is we are not alone
in this world.

279
00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:43.485
[eerie warbling]

280
00:11:43.528 --> 00:11:45.226
-[warbling stops]
-[stammers, shushes]

281
00:11:45.269 --> 00:11:47.750
There are other kinds
of Trolls.

282
00:11:47.794 --> 00:11:49.578
-TROLL: What?
-Wow. That's...

283
00:11:49.621 --> 00:11:50.666
Dad, that's great.

284
00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.537
The more Trolls, the merrier.

285
00:11:52.581 --> 00:11:54.191
You don't understand.

286
00:11:54.235 --> 00:11:56.237
These other Trolls
aren't like us.

287
00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.239
They're different.

288
00:11:58.282 --> 00:11:59.936
Different how?

289
00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:01.068
Different like Legsly?

290
00:12:01.111 --> 00:12:02.460
I love being me.

291
00:12:02.504 --> 00:12:03.940
-Or Fuzzbert? Or Smidge?
-[Fuzzbert babbling]

292
00:12:03.984 --> 00:12:05.028
Or Skyscraper Troll?

293
00:12:05.072 --> 00:12:07.117
[in unison]:
Yeah, different like me?

294
00:12:07.161 --> 00:12:08.728
No, it's not that.

295
00:12:08.771 --> 00:12:11.774
They're different in ways
you can't even imagine.

296
00:12:11.818 --> 00:12:13.950
-[vocalizing pop music]
-You see, we love music

297
00:12:13.994 --> 00:12:16.387
with a hummable hook,
with an upbeat melody,

298
00:12:16.431 --> 00:12:19.347
with a catchy rhythm that makes
you want to snap your fingers,

299
00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:21.828
tap your toes
and wiggle your butt.

300
00:12:21.871 --> 00:12:22.872
That's our music.

301
00:12:22.916 --> 00:12:25.701
That's what makes us
Pop Trolls.

302
00:12:25.745 --> 00:12:27.398
-Ooh.
-It is. -Yes.

303
00:12:27.442 --> 00:12:29.792
But these other Trolls,
they sing different.

304
00:12:29.836 --> 00:12:31.098
-[gasping]
-They dance different.

305
00:12:31.141 --> 00:12:33.578
Why, some of them
can't even begin to grasp

306
00:12:33.622 --> 00:12:36.190
the concept of Hammer Time.

307
00:12:36.233 --> 00:12:38.540
["U Can't Touch This" playing]

308
00:12:38.583 --> 00:12:40.107
You can't touch that!

309
00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.151
[screaming]

310
00:12:41.195 --> 00:12:43.371
[Trolls clamoring]

311
00:12:43.414 --> 00:12:45.460
-[crying]
-[crying]

312
00:12:45.503 --> 00:12:46.722
[screaming]

313
00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:48.680
-♪ Stop.
-[music and clamoring stop]

314
00:12:49.812 --> 00:12:53.076
How about we break down
to a smaller group?

315
00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.122
[birds chirping]

316
00:12:57.167 --> 00:13:00.475
It's a story as old as time.

317
00:13:00.518 --> 00:13:01.737
[clears throat]

318
00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:04.696
In the beginning,
there was silence.

319
00:13:07.264 --> 00:13:08.875
[singsongy]:
Boring.

320
00:13:08.918 --> 00:13:11.399
KING PEPPY: Until one day,
someone made a sound.

321
00:13:11.442 --> 00:13:12.966
-[plays note]
-[Trolls oohing]

322
00:13:13.009 --> 00:13:15.882
Our ancestors were
so inspired by the sound,

323
00:13:15.925 --> 00:13:18.406
-they took six strings.
-[melody plays]

324
00:13:18.449 --> 00:13:23.150
And those six strings had the power to control all music.

325
00:13:23.193 --> 00:13:24.542
They could play anything.

326
00:13:24.586 --> 00:13:26.196
[harp strumming]

327
00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.329
-[different styles playing]
-Techno, funk, classical,

328
00:13:28.372 --> 00:13:30.897
country, hard rock and pop.

329
00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:33.682
And every kind of music
in between.

330
00:13:33.725 --> 00:13:35.423
There was something
for everyone.

331
00:13:35.466 --> 00:13:37.120
It was one big party.

332
00:13:37.164 --> 00:13:38.469
TROLLS:
Yay!

333
00:13:38.513 --> 00:13:40.036
KING PEPPY:
But little by little,

334
00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:42.560
Trolls became intolerant
of each other's music.

335
00:13:42.604 --> 00:13:43.866
-[Trolls arguing]
-TROLL: I want it!

336
00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:46.086
-I want to listen to techno!
-No fair!

337
00:13:46.129 --> 00:13:47.870
Hey, y'all, I want country.

338
00:13:47.914 --> 00:13:50.264
KING PEPPY: They fought
over what kind of music

339
00:13:50.307 --> 00:13:51.874
the strings would play.

340
00:13:51.918 --> 00:13:54.529
The elders realized
there was but one solution.

341
00:13:54.572 --> 00:13:56.748
TROLLS: Blah,
blah-blah-blah-blah. Agreed.

342
00:13:56.792 --> 00:13:59.273
KING PEPPY:
Each tribe would take a string

343
00:13:59.316 --> 00:14:01.753
-and go their separate ways.
-[Trolls chattering]

344
00:14:03.364 --> 00:14:07.498
Those six tribes have lived
in isolation ever since.

345
00:14:07.542 --> 00:14:10.284
Techno, Country, Rock,

346
00:14:10.327 --> 00:14:12.286
Classical, Funk,

347
00:14:12.329 --> 00:14:15.115
and us, the Pop Trolls.

348
00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.596
Now Barb's announcement
makes sense.

349
00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:20.076
She wants to reunite
the strings

350
00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:22.818
so the Troll World
can be one big party again.

351
00:14:22.862 --> 00:14:24.341
Wait, that's all you heard?

352
00:14:24.385 --> 00:14:26.126
-One big party?
-[chuckles]: Yeah!

353
00:14:26.169 --> 00:14:28.084
It's when all the Trolls
lived in harmony.

354
00:14:28.128 --> 00:14:30.565
And what's more important
than living in harmony?

355
00:14:30.608 --> 00:14:31.871
Well, I heard fighting.

356
00:14:31.914 --> 00:14:33.350
The strings together
leads to fighting.

357
00:14:33.394 --> 00:14:34.656
KING PEPPY:
Exactly, Branch.

358
00:14:34.699 --> 00:14:37.354
That's why we need
to keep our string safe.

359
00:14:37.398 --> 00:14:39.617
♪

360
00:14:43.273 --> 00:14:44.274
Behold!

361
00:14:44.318 --> 00:14:47.016
The pop music string.

362
00:14:47.060 --> 00:14:50.019
FEMALE STRING VOICE:
♪ Oh, yeah.

363
00:14:50.063 --> 00:14:52.500
-[Trolls gasping]
-[magic jingling]

364
00:14:55.111 --> 00:14:56.939
It's beautiful.

365
00:14:56.983 --> 00:14:58.506
KING PEPPY:
And powerful.

366
00:14:58.549 --> 00:15:01.901
Which is why we can't let it
fall into the wrong hands.

367
00:15:01.944 --> 00:15:04.251
And we won't.
Not on my watch.

368
00:15:04.294 --> 00:15:06.644
What we need is a plan.

369
00:15:06.688 --> 00:15:07.907
Don't worry.

370
00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:10.997
I've been preparing
for this day for years.

371
00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.476
-We run.
-Run?

372
00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.477
And hide.

373
00:15:13.521 --> 00:15:15.088
On it.

374
00:15:15.131 --> 00:15:18.178
But we don't even know what
we're running and hiding from.

375
00:15:18.221 --> 00:15:21.833
We're hiding from Barb and
all the other different Trolls.

376
00:15:21.877 --> 00:15:23.661
POPPY:
You're assuming the worst about

377
00:15:23.705 --> 00:15:25.228
someone you haven't even met.

378
00:15:25.272 --> 00:15:28.579
-You're not listening to me.
-You're not listening to me.

379
00:15:28.623 --> 00:15:31.365
-I'm your father!
-And I'm the queen.

380
00:15:31.408 --> 00:15:32.975
Uh, father trumps queen.

381
00:15:33.019 --> 00:15:35.673
Now, there's no time
to debate this. Let's go.

382
00:15:35.717 --> 00:15:37.414
Come along, Branch.

383
00:15:37.458 --> 00:15:39.199
Well, I, um...

384
00:15:40.243 --> 00:15:42.419
We're all Trolls.

385
00:15:42.463 --> 00:15:44.682
Differences don't matter.

386
00:15:45.596 --> 00:15:46.858
[growling]

387
00:15:46.902 --> 00:15:48.860
Oh, look how cute you are!

388
00:15:48.904 --> 00:15:50.993
Barb is gonna love
your new look.

389
00:15:51.037 --> 00:15:52.908
Tell her I look forward
to helping her

390
00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:54.518
plan the world's biggest party.

391
00:15:54.562 --> 00:15:55.606
-Poppy.
-[screams]

392
00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.565
-What are you doing?
-Oh. Nothing.

393
00:15:57.608 --> 00:15:59.001
SHEILA B:
Ooh!

394
00:15:59.045 --> 00:16:01.438
Poppy's busted.

395
00:16:01.482 --> 00:16:02.483
[shushing]

396
00:16:02.526 --> 00:16:04.267
BRANCH:
Sneaking out to meet Barb?

397
00:16:04.311 --> 00:16:05.529
Headed into enemy territory?

398
00:16:05.573 --> 00:16:06.530
She's not the enemy.

399
00:16:06.574 --> 00:16:08.315
She's a queen, the same as me.

400
00:16:08.358 --> 00:16:10.317
-[growling]
-[grunting]

401
00:16:11.231 --> 00:16:12.623
Bye-bye, little bat.

402
00:16:12.667 --> 00:16:15.191
Your dad just told us
that Queen Barb is bad news.

403
00:16:15.235 --> 00:16:16.671
Well, my dad
doesn't know everything.

404
00:16:16.714 --> 00:16:18.281
He knows more about this.

405
00:16:18.325 --> 00:16:20.544
You didn't even know there was
a string until this morning.

406
00:16:20.588 --> 00:16:23.199
He may be fine in a world where
everybody lives in isolation,

407
00:16:23.243 --> 00:16:25.114
-but I'm not.
-Well, but we don't know

408
00:16:25.158 --> 00:16:27.421
anything about
the other Trolls.

409
00:16:27.464 --> 00:16:28.988
Well, we know they're Trolls.

410
00:16:29.031 --> 00:16:30.772
Branch, look around
Troll Village.

411
00:16:30.815 --> 00:16:33.209
Everybody's different, even us.

412
00:16:33.253 --> 00:16:35.211
[distant sneeze]

413
00:16:35.255 --> 00:16:36.212
Oh.

414
00:16:36.256 --> 00:16:37.648
Did you hear something?

415
00:16:37.692 --> 00:16:39.346
Stop trying
to change the subject.

416
00:16:39.389 --> 00:16:41.565
Look, being queen means
having a lot of power,

417
00:16:41.609 --> 00:16:43.959
and it's my job
to use it for good.

418
00:16:44.003 --> 00:16:45.569
I can't stay home
when I know there's

419
00:16:45.613 --> 00:16:49.182
a world full of different
Trolls out there just like us.

420
00:16:50.052 --> 00:16:52.185
[sighs] This is a terrible idea

421
00:16:52.228 --> 00:16:54.926
that will most likely
blow up in your face.

422
00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:56.928
-Okay, bye.
-What?

423
00:17:03.413 --> 00:17:04.980
[groans]

424
00:17:09.115 --> 00:17:10.116
[grunts]

425
00:17:10.159 --> 00:17:12.814
And I guess
I'm coming with you.

426
00:17:12.857 --> 00:17:14.816
[sobs]:
Oh! Thank you.

427
00:17:14.859 --> 00:17:17.036
I really didn't want
to go by myself.

428
00:17:17.079 --> 00:17:19.255
-Road trip!
-Yeah!

429
00:17:24.565 --> 00:17:26.784
♪

430
00:17:38.274 --> 00:17:40.407
They areall different.

431
00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:44.324
[gasps softly] A-And this one
looks a little bit like me.

432
00:17:46.152 --> 00:17:47.370
[gasps]

433
00:17:47.414 --> 00:17:49.068
We even have the same hat!

434
00:17:49.111 --> 00:17:51.679
[echoing]: ...same hat,
same hat, same hat!

435
00:17:51.722 --> 00:17:53.333
♪

436
00:18:10.698 --> 00:18:12.613
Goodbye.

437
00:18:12.656 --> 00:18:15.094
I hope I see you again,
friends.

438
00:18:15.137 --> 00:18:18.706
But even though it's scary,
I have to go out there

439
00:18:18.749 --> 00:18:21.752
and see if there's
other Trolls like me.

440
00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.886
[shrieks]

441
00:18:24.929 --> 00:18:27.018
Oh, man, this is gonna be hard.

442
00:18:27.062 --> 00:18:29.499
-BARB: All aboard!
-["Crazy Train" playing]

443
00:18:29.543 --> 00:18:30.718
[laughing]

444
00:18:30.761 --> 00:18:32.981
♪ Ai, ai, ai

445
00:18:33.895 --> 00:18:36.115
[rock music playing loudly]

446
00:18:37.464 --> 00:18:39.596
♪ Crazy

447
00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:42.382
♪ But that's how it goes

448
00:18:44.123 --> 00:18:46.516
♪ Millions of people

449
00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:49.389
♪ Living as foes

450
00:18:51.217 --> 00:18:53.132
♪ Music

451
00:18:53.175 --> 00:18:56.178
♪ Has kept us apart

452
00:18:57.745 --> 00:19:00.051
♪ It's time for the hard rock

453
00:19:00.095 --> 00:19:03.142
♪ Revolution to start

454
00:19:04.404 --> 00:19:08.059
♪ No spats, no tiffs,
no fighting ♪

455
00:19:08.103 --> 00:19:10.801
♪ When everyone's the same

456
00:19:11.628 --> 00:19:13.761
♪ I'm going off the rails

457
00:19:13.804 --> 00:19:19.549
♪ On a crazy train!

458
00:19:19.593 --> 00:19:22.987
-Yeah! I got the Techno string!
-[excited chatter]

459
00:19:23.031 --> 00:19:25.381
Who knew world domination
could be so much fun?

460
00:19:25.425 --> 00:19:28.428
-Yeah! -All right, Barb!
-[Trolls cheering]

461
00:19:28.471 --> 00:19:29.429
All right!

462
00:19:29.472 --> 00:19:30.778
[both yell]

463
00:19:30.821 --> 00:19:33.215
Ha! Queen Barb!

464
00:19:33.259 --> 00:19:34.912
[both laugh]

465
00:19:34.956 --> 00:19:37.524
[heavy electric guitar
chord plays]

466
00:19:39.787 --> 00:19:42.398
[electric guitar riff plays]

467
00:19:42.442 --> 00:19:47.011
Only four more strings to go
until rock unites the world.

468
00:19:47.055 --> 00:19:48.012
[excited chatter]

469
00:19:48.056 --> 00:19:49.797
Dad? Where's Dad?

470
00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:52.234
[toilet flushes]

471
00:19:52.278 --> 00:19:54.454
-♪
-[engine revving]

472
00:19:58.893 --> 00:20:00.286
There you are, Dad.

473
00:20:00.329 --> 00:20:02.462
-I got the Techno string.
-Cool.

474
00:20:02.505 --> 00:20:04.333
-What's a string ag-again?
-[back-up alarm beeping]

475
00:20:04.377 --> 00:20:05.465
What? Uh...

476
00:20:05.508 --> 00:20:07.118
-Don't you remember the plan?
-Plan?

477
00:20:07.162 --> 00:20:09.120
-I don't remember... [mumbles]
-Oh.

478
00:20:09.164 --> 00:20:10.339
-Great idea, man.
-Whoa.

479
00:20:10.383 --> 00:20:11.427
Okay, guys, line up.

480
00:20:11.471 --> 00:20:12.907
We're gonna go over
the plan again.

481
00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:13.951
[Trolls murmur, chuckle]

482
00:20:13.995 --> 00:20:16.563
Okay. We're on a World Tour.

483
00:20:16.606 --> 00:20:19.609
And on each stop,
we get a new string.

484
00:20:19.653 --> 00:20:21.132
When I have all six strings,

485
00:20:21.176 --> 00:20:23.744
I'll play the ultimate
power chord.

486
00:20:23.787 --> 00:20:25.136
[electric guitar chord plays]

487
00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:28.966
And I will unite the Trolls
under one music.

488
00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:30.272
Our music!

489
00:20:30.316 --> 00:20:31.969
-TROLLS: Rock!
-[excited chatter]

490
00:20:34.842 --> 00:20:36.409
Oh, here it comes.

491
00:20:39.934 --> 00:20:42.632
[grunting slowly]

492
00:20:42.676 --> 00:20:44.678
Uh, just a little bit more.

493
00:20:44.721 --> 00:20:46.114
Riff, just help him, man.

494
00:20:46.157 --> 00:20:47.333
Yes, Your Rockness.

495
00:20:47.376 --> 00:20:48.725
Aw.

496
00:20:48.769 --> 00:20:49.813
There it is.

497
00:20:49.857 --> 00:20:51.815
-[Trolls cheering]
-BARB: Yeah!

498
00:20:51.859 --> 00:20:53.513
-Rock and roll!
-Yeah!

499
00:20:53.556 --> 00:20:54.644
[both laugh]

500
00:20:54.688 --> 00:20:55.863
Yeah!

501
00:20:59.867 --> 00:21:01.651
[inhales deeply]

502
00:21:01.695 --> 00:21:03.523
-[sighs]
-All right.

503
00:21:03.566 --> 00:21:07.266
In a short 456 pages, I'm gonna
know how to fly this thing.

504
00:21:07.309 --> 00:21:08.963
-[knuckles crack]
-Ugh, Branch,

505
00:21:09.006 --> 00:21:11.052
we don't need
a giant, comprehensive manual.

506
00:21:11.095 --> 00:21:12.358
-[grunts]
-[gasps]

507
00:21:12.401 --> 00:21:13.620
How hard can it be?
♪ Doo-doo-doo-doo-doo.

508
00:21:13.663 --> 00:21:16.187
-[console beeping]
-♪ Try one of these.

509
00:21:16.231 --> 00:21:19.974
[Sheila B whooping, laughing]

510
00:21:20.017 --> 00:21:21.802
All right, Poppy!

511
00:21:21.845 --> 00:21:23.325
Easy on the buttons!

512
00:21:23.369 --> 00:21:24.370
-Sorry.
-[snoring nearby]

513
00:21:24.413 --> 00:21:26.502
[shushes]
What was that?

514
00:21:26.546 --> 00:21:27.503
[sleepy murmur]

515
00:21:27.547 --> 00:21:29.505
[whistling exhale]

516
00:21:29.549 --> 00:21:30.680
[sleepy murmur]

517
00:21:30.724 --> 00:21:31.855
[snoring]

518
00:21:31.899 --> 00:21:33.509
[Mr. Dinkles sucking, cooing]

519
00:21:33.553 --> 00:21:34.858
Biggie?

520
00:21:34.902 --> 00:21:36.120
Oh, hello.

521
00:21:36.164 --> 00:21:37.861
Sorry. I couldn't help myself.

522
00:21:37.905 --> 00:21:39.689
You know how I am
around cotton candy.

523
00:21:39.733 --> 00:21:40.864
-[burps]
-Oh, dear.

524
00:21:40.908 --> 00:21:41.865
Now look what's happened.

525
00:21:41.909 --> 00:21:44.346
Mr. Dinkles got all gummed up.

526
00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:45.913
-[squeaks]
-[gasps] Mr. Dinkles!

527
00:21:45.956 --> 00:21:47.088
Mr. Dinkles!

528
00:21:47.131 --> 00:21:48.350
Oh, there you are.
I thought you were--

529
00:21:48.394 --> 00:21:50.831
Oh. Right, then.
We'll just be on our way--

530
00:21:50.874 --> 00:21:52.223
[screams] Hey!

531
00:21:52.267 --> 00:21:54.748
Poppy, wh-where are you
balloon-flying us to?

532
00:21:54.791 --> 00:21:57.272
We're on a mission
to help Barb unite the Trolls,

533
00:21:57.316 --> 00:21:59.535
and I'm so glad
you're coming with us.

534
00:21:59.579 --> 00:22:00.884
I did what in the who now?

535
00:22:00.928 --> 00:22:02.321
Hey, man, join the club.

536
00:22:02.364 --> 00:22:04.366
And I hope you didn't eat
all the cotton candy,

537
00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:06.325
because Barb is gonna love it.

538
00:22:06.368 --> 00:22:07.935
[clears throat]
Branchifer?

539
00:22:07.978 --> 00:22:09.197
[clears throat]
Y-Yes, Poppifer?

540
00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:11.199
-What is this?
-Oh, it's nothing, nothing.

541
00:22:11.242 --> 00:22:13.157
-That-that-that-that's
just my man stuff. -[gasps]

542
00:22:13.201 --> 00:22:14.507
I love man stuff!

543
00:22:14.550 --> 00:22:16.378
Weapons?

544
00:22:16.422 --> 00:22:18.119
Ugh. For shame.

545
00:22:18.162 --> 00:22:19.338
Well, I-I...

546
00:22:19.381 --> 00:22:21.122
Violence never solves
a problem, Branch.

547
00:22:21.165 --> 00:22:22.906
-[squeaks]
-[shrieks]

548
00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:24.908
I'm not saying
we have to use them.

549
00:22:24.952 --> 00:22:26.736
I'm just saying
it's better to be prepared

550
00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.390
in case we need them.

551
00:22:28.434 --> 00:22:31.262
We won't need them unless these
pointy sticks help you listen

552
00:22:31.306 --> 00:22:32.960
or these rocks help you
put yourself

553
00:22:33.003 --> 00:22:34.222
in someone else's shoes.

554
00:22:34.265 --> 00:22:35.745
And what about these?
Is this-- What, I--

555
00:22:35.789 --> 00:22:36.964
Is this some kind of jewelry?

556
00:22:37.007 --> 00:22:37.921
Oh, it's actually
kind of cool-looking.

557
00:22:37.965 --> 00:22:38.922
♪ Oh.

558
00:22:38.966 --> 00:22:40.315
Gi-Give me that.

559
00:22:40.359 --> 00:22:43.187
We don't even know
what's out there.

560
00:22:46.582 --> 00:22:49.063
Wait! No-- Oh, man.

561
00:22:49.106 --> 00:22:51.631
By the way,
I whittled those for hours.

562
00:22:51.674 --> 00:22:56.375
Branch, the only weapons we
need are this guy and this guy,

563
00:22:56.418 --> 00:22:57.463
for hugs!

564
00:22:57.506 --> 00:23:00.117
Uh, you may want
to take a look at this.

565
00:23:00.161 --> 00:23:02.337
♪

566
00:23:05.035 --> 00:23:07.081
[fire crackling softly]

567
00:23:08.082 --> 00:23:11.128
This is gonna take
a lot of hugs.

568
00:23:11.172 --> 00:23:13.392
♪

569
00:23:25.012 --> 00:23:26.143
Whoa.

570
00:23:26.187 --> 00:23:28.450
Something gnarly happened here.

571
00:23:28.494 --> 00:23:30.147
PENNYWHISTLE:
Hello?

572
00:23:30.191 --> 00:23:31.801
Who said that?

573
00:23:31.845 --> 00:23:34.325
Identify yourself!

574
00:23:34.369 --> 00:23:39.113
PENNYWHISTLE: Uh, are you nice
or are you mean?

575
00:23:39.156 --> 00:23:41.245
W-We're nice.
We're really nice.

576
00:23:41.289 --> 00:23:43.247
Yeah, but not too nice.

577
00:23:43.291 --> 00:23:46.207
So don't even try it.

578
00:23:48.035 --> 00:23:49.515
Okay.

579
00:23:54.084 --> 00:23:55.608
[softly]:
Oh. Hi.

580
00:23:55.651 --> 00:23:57.479
What is this place?

581
00:23:57.523 --> 00:24:00.830
It used to be called
Symphonyville.

582
00:24:00.874 --> 00:24:02.223
[coughs]

583
00:24:02.266 --> 00:24:05.008
Where the Classical Music
Trolls lived.

584
00:24:05.052 --> 00:24:09.230
But that was in the before.

585
00:24:09.273 --> 00:24:10.753
What happened here?

586
00:24:10.797 --> 00:24:16.280
Well, it was the most wonderful
place you ever did seen.

587
00:24:16.324 --> 00:24:18.892
[lively classical music
playing, chatter, laughter]

588
00:24:18.935 --> 00:24:20.720
It was a place where all of

589
00:24:20.763 --> 00:24:25.159
the Classical Music Trolls
could live in perfect harmony.

590
00:24:25.202 --> 00:24:27.422
[classical music continues]

591
00:24:28.249 --> 00:24:29.859
[laughs]:
Ooh.

592
00:24:29.903 --> 00:24:33.559
Wherever the conductor led,
we followed.

593
00:24:33.602 --> 00:24:36.431
Play, play. [vocalizes]
Beautiful.

594
00:24:36.475 --> 00:24:39.956
-[laughs] -But then Queen Barb showed up.

595
00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:41.044
Oh, no.

596
00:24:41.088 --> 00:24:42.698
'Sup, Trollzart dude?

597
00:24:42.742 --> 00:24:44.831
I'm here for your string.

598
00:24:44.874 --> 00:24:46.876
We will not go quietly.

599
00:24:46.920 --> 00:24:48.704
[playing Beethoven's
"Symphony No. 5 in C Minor"]

600
00:24:48.748 --> 00:24:50.184
-[triangle dings]
-[Barb snores]

601
00:24:50.227 --> 00:24:51.838
[sighs]:
Mi, mi, mi, mi, mi.

602
00:24:51.881 --> 00:24:54.536
Oh. Oh, I'm sorry,
I-I must have fallen asleep,

603
00:24:54.580 --> 00:24:57.539
because your music
is so boring.

604
00:24:57.583 --> 00:24:58.584
[scoffs]

605
00:24:58.627 --> 00:25:00.063
Where are the words, bro?
Right?

606
00:25:00.107 --> 00:25:01.325
Now give me your string.

607
00:25:01.369 --> 00:25:03.632
[amplifier buzzes, hums]

608
00:25:03.676 --> 00:25:06.069
[playing Beethoven's
"Symphony No. 5 in C Minor"]

609
00:25:06.113 --> 00:25:08.202
-Oh! Oh!
-[Trolls gasping]

610
00:25:09.029 --> 00:25:11.161
[sighs] No.

611
00:25:12.293 --> 00:25:14.251
PENNYWHISTLE:
She took our string.

612
00:25:14.295 --> 00:25:15.426
Our-our music.

613
00:25:15.470 --> 00:25:18.952
She took everyone.

614
00:25:18.995 --> 00:25:20.867
[wind whistling softly]

615
00:25:20.910 --> 00:25:24.305
We lost everything.

616
00:25:27.003 --> 00:25:29.353
Barb doesn't want to unite us.

617
00:25:30.441 --> 00:25:32.618
She wants to destroy us.

618
00:25:40.321 --> 00:25:43.454
We need to make sure
our own string is safe.

619
00:25:43.498 --> 00:25:46.457
Uh, our string is safe.

620
00:25:46.501 --> 00:25:47.458
What?!

621
00:25:47.502 --> 00:25:48.938
Poppy, are-are you crazy?

622
00:25:48.982 --> 00:25:50.940
I thought it was a good idea
at the time.

623
00:25:50.984 --> 00:25:54.465
I-I can't believe another queen
would use her power for evil.

624
00:25:54.509 --> 00:25:55.771
Okay. Change of plans.

625
00:25:55.815 --> 00:25:57.468
We need to get home
as fast as we can

626
00:25:57.512 --> 00:25:58.731
and get everyone in the bunker.

627
00:25:58.774 --> 00:26:00.559
Uh, no. Change of plans.

628
00:26:00.602 --> 00:26:02.952
We have to stop Barb
from destroying all music.

629
00:26:02.996 --> 00:26:04.737
If we don't stop her, who will?

630
00:26:04.780 --> 00:26:06.608
Poppy, you said this could be
handled with hugs.

631
00:26:06.652 --> 00:26:09.045
How are we gonna hug
our way out of this one?

632
00:26:09.089 --> 00:26:10.264
-It's okay, Biggie.
-Really?

633
00:26:10.307 --> 00:26:11.874
It's okay to be terrified?

634
00:26:11.918 --> 00:26:13.963
When am I gonna learn to stay
away from the cotton candy?!

635
00:26:14.007 --> 00:26:14.964
No.

636
00:26:15.008 --> 00:26:16.400
As your queen,

637
00:26:16.444 --> 00:26:19.229
I promise that I will
protect you, no matter what.

638
00:26:19.273 --> 00:26:22.929
I... pinky promise.

639
00:26:22.972 --> 00:26:24.844
[gasps]

640
00:26:24.887 --> 00:26:29.457
Poppy, you know you can't
go back on a pinky promise.

641
00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:31.981
Never did, never will.

642
00:26:32.025 --> 00:26:35.289
♪

643
00:26:35.332 --> 00:26:37.073
-[electricity crackles]
-[magic jingling]

644
00:26:37.117 --> 00:26:39.336
[wind whooshing]

645
00:26:42.122 --> 00:26:43.993
[laughs]

646
00:26:44.037 --> 00:26:45.429
Farewell!

647
00:26:48.650 --> 00:26:50.826
A pinky promise.

648
00:26:50.870 --> 00:26:52.306
Dang.

649
00:26:55.352 --> 00:26:57.137
Let it be so.

650
00:26:57.180 --> 00:26:59.705
And so it is.

651
00:26:59.748 --> 00:27:00.836
[groans]

652
00:27:00.880 --> 00:27:03.447
This just got real.

653
00:27:03.491 --> 00:27:05.232
POPPY: We have to get to
the Country Music Trolls

654
00:27:05.275 --> 00:27:07.800
in Lonesome Flats
before Barb does.

655
00:27:07.843 --> 00:27:09.540
Will you come with us?

656
00:27:09.584 --> 00:27:10.498
Oh, no.

657
00:27:10.541 --> 00:27:12.892
Someone has to rebuild.

658
00:27:12.935 --> 00:27:18.332
And Pennywhistle is
that woodwind for the job.

659
00:27:19.159 --> 00:27:20.769
[grunts]

660
00:27:27.254 --> 00:27:28.995
Good luck, little Pennywhistle.

661
00:27:30.039 --> 00:27:32.259
Goodbye, Poppy.

662
00:27:35.610 --> 00:27:36.785
[sighs]

663
00:27:37.656 --> 00:27:39.919
[whooping, excited shouting]

664
00:27:39.962 --> 00:27:42.661
[growling]

665
00:27:43.749 --> 00:27:45.881
Wait. Is that...

666
00:27:45.925 --> 00:27:47.100
-Debbie?
-Oh, what?

667
00:27:47.143 --> 00:27:48.579
-Oh, that's a lot of glitter.
-BARB: No!

668
00:27:48.623 --> 00:27:50.669
What did they do to you,
my hairy little baby?!

669
00:27:50.712 --> 00:27:51.887
Come here, come here,
come here.

670
00:27:51.931 --> 00:27:53.410
-Gnarly.
-What-what-what do you...

671
00:27:53.454 --> 00:27:55.238
-What is this?
-What, what...

672
00:27:55.282 --> 00:27:56.892
Pop Trolls?

673
00:27:56.936 --> 00:27:57.980
[clears throat]

674
00:27:58.024 --> 00:28:00.722
"Dear Barb,
can't wait to meet you.

675
00:28:00.766 --> 00:28:03.333
I have tons of
great party ideas."

676
00:28:03.377 --> 00:28:04.726
I like that.

677
00:28:04.770 --> 00:28:07.511
"Maybe you and I
can even be best friends."

678
00:28:07.555 --> 00:28:08.904
Best friends?

679
00:28:08.948 --> 00:28:10.950
Is she making fun of me?

680
00:28:10.993 --> 00:28:12.908
No one says that.

681
00:28:12.952 --> 00:28:15.911
Friendship takes time and years
of mutual care and respect.

682
00:28:15.955 --> 00:28:17.783
You don't just become
best friends.

683
00:28:17.826 --> 00:28:21.743
Plus, everyone knows I already
have a ton of friends.

684
00:28:21.787 --> 00:28:22.875
Like Carol.

685
00:28:22.918 --> 00:28:24.485
Right, Carol?

686
00:28:25.573 --> 00:28:27.488
Okay, you're busy.
That's fine.

687
00:28:27.531 --> 00:28:28.489
Love you, Carol.

688
00:28:28.532 --> 00:28:30.796
[quiet crackling]

689
00:28:33.886 --> 00:28:36.627
POPPY [over speaker]:
♪ Trolls just wanna have fun.

690
00:28:36.671 --> 00:28:37.585
[growls]

691
00:28:37.628 --> 00:28:39.282
-Gnarly.
-[back-up alarm beeping]

692
00:28:39.326 --> 00:28:41.763
Pop music isn't even
real music!

693
00:28:41.807 --> 00:28:44.940
It's bland! It's repetitive!

694
00:28:44.984 --> 00:28:47.116
The lyrics are empty!

695
00:28:47.160 --> 00:28:51.120
Worst of all, it crawls into
your head like an earworm!

696
00:28:51.164 --> 00:28:53.775
[chain saw buzzing]

697
00:28:53.819 --> 00:28:55.255
[sighs]

698
00:28:55.298 --> 00:28:57.474
You know, and you can't
get it out-- Uh, I'm tired now.

699
00:28:57.518 --> 00:29:00.216
[whoops] Hating things
takes a lot of energy.

700
00:29:00.260 --> 00:29:02.784
♪ Trolls just wanna have fun

701
00:29:02.828 --> 00:29:04.438
-♪ Trolls just wanna...
-No. No.

702
00:29:04.481 --> 00:29:05.874
Look what their music
just did to Dad.

703
00:29:05.918 --> 00:29:07.310
-Daddy? Come back.
-[slurping]

704
00:29:07.354 --> 00:29:08.747
Come back to me, Daddy.

705
00:29:09.922 --> 00:29:11.662
Nice hair, dude.

706
00:29:11.706 --> 00:29:13.664
No one does this to Dad.

707
00:29:13.708 --> 00:29:15.971
And no one makes fun
of Queen Barb.

708
00:29:16.015 --> 00:29:16.842
[humming]

709
00:29:16.885 --> 00:29:19.540
Ah! I need that Pop string.

710
00:29:19.583 --> 00:29:21.847
And I know who's gonna help me.

711
00:29:21.890 --> 00:29:25.415
The most feared bounty hunters
in all of Trolldom.

712
00:29:25.459 --> 00:29:27.504
-[smooth jazz music playing]
-[bell dings]

713
00:29:27.548 --> 00:29:30.812
Chaz, the Smooth Jazz Troll.

714
00:29:30.856 --> 00:29:32.988
-["Mi Gente" playing]
-The Reggaeton Trolls.

715
00:29:33.032 --> 00:29:35.077
-["Russian Roulette" playing]
-♪ La, la-la-la...

716
00:29:35.121 --> 00:29:37.210
BARB:
The K-Pop Gang.

717
00:29:37.253 --> 00:29:39.647
-["Hocus Pocus" playing,
singer yodeling] -And...

718
00:29:39.690 --> 00:29:41.214
the Yodelers.

719
00:29:41.257 --> 00:29:42.215
Okay.

720
00:29:42.258 --> 00:29:43.825
As you probably know,

721
00:29:43.869 --> 00:29:46.915
I'm bringing a tidal wave of
rock across this land of ours.

722
00:29:46.959 --> 00:29:48.874
♪

723
00:29:48.917 --> 00:29:51.180
And soon there will be
nothing but hard rock

724
00:29:51.224 --> 00:29:53.008
as far as the ear can hear.

725
00:29:53.052 --> 00:29:56.098
Whoever brings me Queen Poppy
gets to keep

726
00:29:56.142 --> 00:30:00.102
their very own music
in their very own territory.

727
00:30:00.146 --> 00:30:02.626
Right over here.

728
00:30:02.670 --> 00:30:03.932
-[Trolls murmuring, groaning]
-TROLL: Oh.

729
00:30:03.976 --> 00:30:05.673
I don't know.
It looks pretty tiny.

730
00:30:05.716 --> 00:30:07.066
You want it or not?

731
00:30:08.545 --> 00:30:11.592
All you have to do is
get me Queen Poppy!

732
00:30:11.635 --> 00:30:13.420
-Oh, okay. -Sounds like
a pretty good deal.

733
00:30:13.463 --> 00:30:14.856
Do you validate parking?

734
00:30:14.900 --> 00:30:16.727
Dude, where are the Yodelers?

735
00:30:16.771 --> 00:30:18.729
I heard a rumor, uh,
that they yodeled so hard,

736
00:30:18.773 --> 00:30:20.427
an avalanche fell on 'em.

737
00:30:21.515 --> 00:30:23.169
Or something.

738
00:30:23.212 --> 00:30:25.519
Well, I don't pay you to hear.

739
00:30:25.562 --> 00:30:28.043
Actually, I'm doing this
for college credit.

740
00:30:28.087 --> 00:30:32.091
If anyone can find me
Queen Poppy and her string,

741
00:30:32.134 --> 00:30:34.267
-it's the Yodelers.
-♪ Just wanna have fun...

742
00:30:34.310 --> 00:30:35.834
[music distorts, stops]

743
00:30:39.141 --> 00:30:41.622
This must be where
the Country Music Trolls live.

744
00:30:41.665 --> 00:30:42.928
Well, it looks like
nobody's here.

745
00:30:42.971 --> 00:30:44.581
We're too late.
Time to go home.

746
00:30:44.625 --> 00:30:45.756
Come on, guys, let's go.

747
00:30:45.800 --> 00:30:48.890
There is no "I quit" in "team."

748
00:30:52.154 --> 00:30:54.896
Cock-a-doodle--

749
00:30:54.940 --> 00:30:57.203
Ah, never mind.

750
00:30:57.246 --> 00:30:59.640
[solemn country music playing]

751
00:31:00.467 --> 00:31:01.903
[bell chimes]

752
00:31:04.950 --> 00:31:07.778
♪ We don't hope for

753
00:31:07.822 --> 00:31:10.694
♪ Making things better

754
00:31:11.521 --> 00:31:14.698
♪ All we want is to

755
00:31:14.742 --> 00:31:17.919
♪ Keep it together

756
00:31:17.963 --> 00:31:20.052
-[giggles]
-♪ Every day is a rainy day

757
00:31:20.095 --> 00:31:22.054
-Happy birthday, honey.
-♪ No change in the weather

758
00:31:22.097 --> 00:31:23.969
-Time to get to work.
-[yak breathing noisily]

759
00:31:24.012 --> 00:31:25.187
Okay, Daddy.

760
00:31:25.231 --> 00:31:26.536
-♪ This kind of life
-[milk spraying]

761
00:31:26.580 --> 00:31:28.799
-♪ Has made our hearts
-[children laughing]

762
00:31:28.843 --> 00:31:30.671
-♪ As hard as leather
-Get it.

763
00:31:30.714 --> 00:31:32.716
[playful chatter]

764
00:31:32.760 --> 00:31:33.979
-[tumbleweed yelling]
-[children screaming]

765
00:31:34.022 --> 00:31:36.285
♪ And all these tears
are from ♪

766
00:31:36.329 --> 00:31:40.159
♪ The dust in our eyes

767
00:31:40.202 --> 00:31:41.943
-[Troll crying]
-♪ And all these years

768
00:31:41.987 --> 00:31:43.684
-[tear crying]
-♪ Just keep on

769
00:31:43.727 --> 00:31:47.035
♪ Passing us by

770
00:31:47.079 --> 00:31:50.169
♪ We all know that we're just

