all you want ♪

1267
00:51:38.312 --> 00:51:39.966
♪ But then you took it,
took it all love ♪

1268
00:51:40.009 --> 00:51:41.576
-♪ Took it all
-♪ All love

1269
00:51:41.620 --> 00:51:43.796
-♪ Turn it up louder
-♪ Turn the music up, come on

1270
00:51:43.839 --> 00:51:45.014
♪ Sing along,
get the crowd up ♪

1271
00:51:45.058 --> 00:51:46.799
♪ I get the crowd up, come on

1272
00:51:46.842 --> 00:51:47.800
♪ But then you took it
all love ♪

1273
00:51:47.843 --> 00:51:49.018
♪ Took it all love, come on

1274
00:51:49.062 --> 00:51:50.107
♪ Then forgot all about us

1275
00:51:50.150 --> 00:51:52.544
♪ Oh, but it's all love

1276
00:51:52.587 --> 00:51:54.154
♪ I feel you

1277
00:51:54.198 --> 00:51:57.462
♪ Sounds good in my ear
when I hear it like that ♪

1278
00:51:57.505 --> 00:52:00.421
♪ I feel you, I say I look good
to the mirror ♪

1279
00:52:00.465 --> 00:52:03.250
-♪ And it says it right back
-♪ Nothing says it like that♪

1280
00:52:03.294 --> 00:52:04.338
♪ I feel you

1281
00:52:04.382 --> 00:52:05.905
♪ A little love
wouldn't kill you ♪

1282
00:52:05.948 --> 00:52:07.298
♪ A little love wouldn't
kill you♪

1283
00:52:07.341 --> 00:52:08.908
♪ You really did me wrong,
it was real cruel ♪

1284
00:52:08.951 --> 00:52:09.909
-♪ It was real cruel♪
-♪ Yeah♪

1285
00:52:09.952 --> 00:52:11.650
♪ Had a lot of love
and I still do ♪

1286
00:52:11.693 --> 00:52:12.955
♪ 'Cause I feel you

1287
00:52:12.999 --> 00:52:15.132
♪ Next morning,
the elders were on it ♪

1288
00:52:15.175 --> 00:52:16.872
-♪ Yeah♪
-♪ They saw the warning signs

1289
00:52:16.916 --> 00:52:18.309
-♪ Couldn't ignore it
-[grunts]

1290
00:52:18.352 --> 00:52:21.138
♪ Had to figure out
how to save the way of life ♪

1291
00:52:21.181 --> 00:52:23.792
♪ They had made,
so they made a play ♪

1292
00:52:23.836 --> 00:52:25.533
♪ The Pop Trolls
were coming for it all ♪

1293
00:52:25.577 --> 00:52:27.970
♪ All for one and one for all,
so the only way we saw ♪

1294
00:52:28.014 --> 00:52:30.538
-♪ How we saw it♪ - There was
one thing left to be done ♪

1295
00:52:30.582 --> 00:52:32.627
-♪ What?♪ - Each leader
grabbed a single string ♪

1296
00:52:32.671 --> 00:52:35.108
-♪ And said, "Run!"
-♪ "Run!"

1297
00:52:37.719 --> 00:52:42.550
KING QUINCY: And the Trolls
never lived in harmony again.

1298
00:52:42.594 --> 00:52:47.033
So the Trolls live in isolation
because of what Pop did?

1299
00:52:47.076 --> 00:52:50.079
Pop tried to destroy our music.

1300
00:52:50.123 --> 00:52:52.778
Just like Barb is trying to do.

1301
00:52:52.821 --> 00:52:54.171
I can make it right.

1302
00:52:54.214 --> 00:52:56.085
History's just gonna
keep repeating itself

1303
00:52:56.129 --> 00:52:58.914
until we make everyone realize
that we're all the same.

1304
00:52:58.958 --> 00:53:00.916
But we're not all the same.

1305
00:53:00.960 --> 00:53:03.049
It's why all our strings
are different.

1306
00:53:03.092 --> 00:53:05.443
Because they reflect
our different music.

1307
00:53:05.486 --> 00:53:08.185
Denying our differences

1308
00:53:08.228 --> 00:53:11.275
is denying the truth
of who we are.

1309
00:53:13.146 --> 00:53:15.453
I hadn't thought of it
like that.

1310
00:53:15.496 --> 00:53:18.238
-[alarm wailing]
-[gasps]

1311
00:53:18.282 --> 00:53:20.501
Rock has arrived!
It's on!

1312
00:53:21.372 --> 00:53:22.590
Prepare for battle!

1313
00:53:22.634 --> 00:53:24.853
["Move On Up"
by Curtis Mayfield playing]

1314
00:53:25.680 --> 00:53:27.204
[records scratching]

1315
00:53:31.686 --> 00:53:33.384
[over speaker]:
Assemble the crew.

1316
00:53:35.429 --> 00:53:37.344
♪ Bite your lip

1317
00:53:38.215 --> 00:53:41.000
♪ And take a trip

1318
00:53:42.306 --> 00:53:44.264
♪ Though there may be
wet road ahead ♪

1319
00:53:44.308 --> 00:53:46.092
I'm gonna make sure
you get to safety.

1320
00:53:46.135 --> 00:53:48.094
♪ And you cannot slip

1321
00:53:48.921 --> 00:53:50.270
-No. No!
-♪ Move on up

1322
00:53:50.314 --> 00:53:51.750
Let me help you!

1323
00:53:51.793 --> 00:53:53.708
-♪ And keep on...
-[music slows, stops]

1324
00:53:53.752 --> 00:53:54.796
Aw, you kidding me?

1325
00:53:54.840 --> 00:53:57.103
[giggles]

1326
00:53:57.146 --> 00:54:00.062
-Hard Rock cut the power.
-They're fighting dirty.

1327
00:54:00.106 --> 00:54:01.890
-POPPY: Cooper!
-[Trolls clamoring]

1328
00:54:07.156 --> 00:54:08.549
-Hickory.
-HICKORY: Don't worry!

1329
00:54:08.593 --> 00:54:10.551
I'll find you guys.

1330
00:54:10.595 --> 00:54:13.206
Uh, Poppy.

1331
00:54:13.250 --> 00:54:14.816
-[engines revving]
-[rock music playing]

1332
00:54:14.860 --> 00:54:16.514
BARB:
Rock on!

1333
00:54:16.557 --> 00:54:18.298
[Branch whimpering]

1334
00:54:18.342 --> 00:54:20.257
[Poppy grunts]

1335
00:54:24.348 --> 00:54:25.740
No! [grunts]

1336
00:54:25.784 --> 00:54:27.829
We have to get back down there.
There's still hope.

1337
00:54:27.873 --> 00:54:30.179
-We can still fix this.
-Poppy, enough.

1338
00:54:30.223 --> 00:54:32.051
I've listened to you
and I've done it your way,

1339
00:54:32.094 --> 00:54:34.096
and now it's your turn
to listen.

1340
00:54:34.140 --> 00:54:36.185
It's time to get back home.

1341
00:54:36.229 --> 00:54:38.492
I'm not like you.
I can't just give up.

1342
00:54:38.536 --> 00:54:39.711
Give up?

1343
00:54:39.754 --> 00:54:41.495
I want to protect
our friends and family.

1344
00:54:41.539 --> 00:54:45.412
I can't go home until I've
proven myself as a good queen.

1345
00:54:45.456 --> 00:54:47.675
So that's what this is
really all about?

1346
00:54:47.719 --> 00:54:49.155
Why are you so upset?

1347
00:54:49.198 --> 00:54:50.809
Because your dad was right

1348
00:54:50.852 --> 00:54:53.333
and Biggie was right
and Queen Essence was right.

1349
00:54:53.377 --> 00:54:57.337
And I've been backing you up
even when you ignore them.

1350
00:54:59.905 --> 00:55:02.081
But you never listen to me.

1351
00:55:02.124 --> 00:55:04.170
Branch, what are you
talking about?

1352
00:55:04.997 --> 00:55:06.955
You want to be a good queen?

1353
00:55:06.999 --> 00:55:08.827
Good queens actually listen.

1354
00:55:08.870 --> 00:55:11.046
You know what I heard
back there?

1355
00:55:11.090 --> 00:55:13.397
Differences do matter.

1356
00:55:15.573 --> 00:55:18.227
Like-like you and me.

1357
00:55:18.271 --> 00:55:20.839
We're too different
to get along.

1358
00:55:20.882 --> 00:55:23.102
Just like all the other Trolls.

1359
00:55:34.592 --> 00:55:37.072
-We arereally different.
-So different.

1360
00:55:37.116 --> 00:55:38.378
-Completely out of harmony.
-Completely.

1361
00:55:38.422 --> 00:55:39.858
I don't even know
why we're friends.

1362
00:55:39.901 --> 00:55:42.208
Neither do I.

1363
00:55:49.781 --> 00:55:51.870
So...

1364
00:55:51.913 --> 00:55:56.309
why do I care about you more
than anybody else in the world?

1365
00:56:00.008 --> 00:56:02.228
Weird, right?

1366
00:56:05.100 --> 00:56:07.320
♪

1367
00:56:13.326 --> 00:56:18.113
♪ I know your favorite song

1368
00:56:18.157 --> 00:56:22.988
♪ I hear it every day

1369
00:56:23.031 --> 00:56:27.514
♪ Whoever made your smile

1370
00:56:27.558 --> 00:56:32.780
♪ Made it to get in my way

1371
00:56:32.824 --> 00:56:37.263
♪ And every time you laugh

1372
00:56:37.306 --> 00:56:42.224
♪ You make that little sound

1373
00:56:42.268 --> 00:56:46.577
♪ It's just the hardest thing

1374
00:56:46.620 --> 00:56:51.495
♪ To love you
but not know how ♪

1375
00:56:51.538 --> 00:56:55.412
♪ I hate that you're perfect

1376
00:56:56.369 --> 00:57:00.634
♪ You're perfect for me

1377
00:57:02.810 --> 00:57:04.290
♪ What good are words

1378
00:57:04.333 --> 00:57:10.209
♪ When they always
just get in our way? ♪

1379
00:57:12.037 --> 00:57:13.734
♪ And it hurts the most

1380
00:57:13.778 --> 00:57:19.174
♪ Just to know
that you don't feel the same ♪

1381
00:57:19.218 --> 00:57:20.698
♪ The same

1382
00:57:20.741 --> 00:57:22.700
♪ Yeah

1383
00:57:22.743 --> 00:57:26.486
♪ And I hate
that you're perfect ♪

1384
00:57:26.530 --> 00:57:27.487
[bell dings]

1385
00:57:27.531 --> 00:57:31.273
♪ You're perfect for me

1386
00:57:31.317 --> 00:57:32.623
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah♪

1387
00:57:32.666 --> 00:57:36.104
♪ I hate that you're perfect

1388
00:57:37.149 --> 00:57:43.111
♪ You're perfect for me.

1389
00:57:43.155 --> 00:57:44.286
[quiet laugh nearby]

1390
00:57:44.330 --> 00:57:45.200
BABY BUN [whispers]:
I see you, Branch.

1391
00:57:45.244 --> 00:57:46.550
ARI [singsongy]:
Over here.

1392
00:57:46.593 --> 00:57:47.420
-WANI: There he is.
-GOMDORI: Can you see me?

1393
00:57:47.464 --> 00:57:48.508
-[gasps]
-[laughter]

1394
00:57:48.552 --> 00:57:49.727
-[whistle]
-GOMDORI: I can see you.

1395
00:57:49.770 --> 00:57:51.163
-BABY BUN: Let's get him.
-[laughter]

1396
00:57:51.206 --> 00:57:52.512
WANI:
One, two, three.

1397
00:57:52.556 --> 00:57:53.861
-ALL: Yay!
-[gasps, grunts]

1398
00:57:53.905 --> 00:57:54.993
[yells]:
Oh!

1399
00:57:55.036 --> 00:57:56.516
-[gasps]
-["Russian Roulette" playing]

1400
00:57:56.560 --> 00:57:57.517
WANI:
Hey, crybaby.

1401
00:57:57.561 --> 00:57:59.563
-Your name Poppy?
-[laughter]

1402
00:57:59.606 --> 00:58:01.695
What? No.
Who are you guys?

1403
00:58:01.739 --> 00:58:03.523
-We are the K-Pop Gang.
-[whoops]

1404
00:58:03.567 --> 00:58:05.960
And you're going to take us
to Queen Poppy.

1405
00:58:06.004 --> 00:58:06.961
[chuckles]:
What?

1406
00:58:07.005 --> 00:58:09.224
["Mi Gente" playing]

1407
00:58:10.922 --> 00:58:12.053
[music stops]

1408
00:58:12.097 --> 00:58:13.881
-Not so fast, Tracy.
-[giggles]

1409
00:58:13.925 --> 00:58:14.882
We're taking him.

1410
00:58:14.926 --> 00:58:16.536
It's pronounced "Tresillo."

1411
00:58:16.580 --> 00:58:18.669
-If you want him...
-[reggaeton beat plays]

1412
00:58:18.712 --> 00:58:20.714
-you're going to have
to dance for him. -[laughter]

1413
00:58:20.758 --> 00:58:23.848
I can't live in a world
without reggaeton.

1414
00:58:23.891 --> 00:58:26.677
And we can't live in a world
without K-pop.

1415
00:58:26.720 --> 00:58:29.114
-MALE VOICE: Dance-off!
-[dramatic music plays] -Ooh!

1416
00:58:29.157 --> 00:58:32.378
["Russian Roulette" playing,
Trolls singing in Korean]

1417
00:58:34.293 --> 00:58:35.250
♪ Heart-b-b-b-beat

1418
00:58:35.294 --> 00:58:37.514
[singing in Korean]

1419
00:58:39.994 --> 00:58:40.952
♪ Crazy

1420
00:58:40.995 --> 00:58:42.214
[singing in Korean]

1421
00:58:42.257 --> 00:58:44.303
♪ Russian roulette, b-b-beat.

1422
00:58:44.346 --> 00:58:47.306
-["Mi Gente" playing,
singing in Spanish] -[gasps]

1423
00:58:53.051 --> 00:58:54.618
♪ Freeze

1424
00:58:54.661 --> 00:58:56.228
♪

1425
00:58:56.271 --> 00:58:57.621
[screaming, laughing]

1426
00:58:58.535 --> 00:59:01.276
♪ Un, dos, tres, leggo.

1427
00:59:01.320 --> 00:59:02.277
[music stops]

1428
00:59:02.321 --> 00:59:04.018
-Wow. -[giggles]
-Respect.

1429
00:59:04.062 --> 00:59:05.498
-Respect.
-[grunts]

1430
00:59:05.542 --> 00:59:07.326
-Why don't we split him?
-Huh?

1431
00:59:07.369 --> 00:59:08.588
-Good idea. -Yeah.
-[laughter]

1432
00:59:08.632 --> 00:59:10.938
Wait, wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait.

1433
00:59:10.982 --> 00:59:14.768
Why does Barb get to decide
which music gets to be saved?

1434
00:59:14.812 --> 00:59:16.770
All music should be saved.

1435
00:59:18.642 --> 00:59:21.558
All right, okay.
I'm listening, Pop Troll.

1436
00:59:27.781 --> 00:59:31.176
FEMALE STRING VOICE:
♪ Oh, yeah.

1437
00:59:32.003 --> 00:59:33.918
-[gasps]
-[panting]

1438
00:59:33.961 --> 00:59:36.181
Poppy, there you are.

1439
00:59:36.224 --> 00:59:39.619
Hickory!
Oh, it's so good to see you.

1440
00:59:39.663 --> 00:59:40.881
Where's Branch?

1441
00:59:40.925 --> 00:59:42.666
We had a fight.
He's gone.

1442
00:59:42.709 --> 00:59:44.145
He's heading back
to Pop Village.

1443
00:59:44.189 --> 00:59:46.104
[sighs] That's a shame.

1444
00:59:46.147 --> 00:59:47.366
[Poppy sighs]

1445
00:59:47.409 --> 00:59:49.542
I was so desperate
to be a good queen

1446
00:59:49.586 --> 00:59:53.198
that I stopped listening
to anyone but myself.

1447
00:59:54.678 --> 00:59:56.767
Including my best friend.
[sighs]

1448
00:59:56.810 --> 00:59:59.900
And it's all because of
this stupid string.

1449
00:59:59.944 --> 01:00:02.990
-[pop riff echoes]
-[magic jingling]

1450
01:00:03.034 --> 01:00:05.993
Poppy, take the string
and run as fast as you can,

1451
01:00:06.037 --> 01:00:07.081
-you hear me?
-What?

1452
01:00:07.125 --> 01:00:08.343
What are you talking about?

1453
01:00:08.387 --> 01:00:10.824
Trust me, just go.

1454
01:00:10.868 --> 01:00:12.696
Now! Please! Just go!

1455
01:00:12.739 --> 01:00:14.349
-[male voice grunting]
-Hickory, are you all right?

1456
01:00:14.393 --> 01:00:15.960
-I'm fine.
-[male voice grumbling]

1457
01:00:16.003 --> 01:00:17.265
Hey. Hey, now!

1458
01:00:17.309 --> 01:00:18.266
Stop that!

1459
01:00:18.310 --> 01:00:19.398
-[gasps]
-Here.

1460
01:00:19.441 --> 01:00:21.269
-Oh, whoa, whoa!
-[male voice grunting]

1461
01:00:22.096 --> 01:00:23.881
[Poppy shouts, gasps]

1462
01:00:23.924 --> 01:00:26.013
-[grunts]
-[screams]

1463
01:00:26.057 --> 01:00:27.972
-[grunts] Nein!
-[gasps]

1464
01:00:28.015 --> 01:00:29.190
What are you doing, Hickory?!

1465
01:00:29.234 --> 01:00:30.627
-Quiet, Dickory!
-POPPY: What's going on?

1466
01:00:30.670 --> 01:00:33.542
-Hickory?
-I am so sorry.

1467
01:00:33.586 --> 01:00:34.369
[yells]

1468
01:00:34.413 --> 01:00:35.806
DICKORY:
Yeah.

1469
01:00:35.849 --> 01:00:38.591
Show her who you really are,
Hickory!

1470
01:00:42.595 --> 01:00:44.771
["Hocus Pocus" playing,
Dickory yodeling]

1471
01:00:46.773 --> 01:00:48.775
[Hickory vocalizing]

1472
01:00:52.126 --> 01:00:54.085
[sings high-pitched note]

1473
01:00:54.128 --> 01:00:56.391
Wait.

1474
01:00:56.435 --> 01:00:58.045
You're the Yodelers?

1475
01:00:58.089 --> 01:00:59.046
[chuckles]:
Yeah.

1476
01:00:59.090 --> 01:01:00.787
Ya darn skippy, playa-play.

1477
01:01:00.831 --> 01:01:03.181
And you were gonna give
our string to Barb?

1478
01:01:03.224 --> 01:01:07.228
Ding, ding. Give this person a
strudel for the correct answer.

1479
01:01:07.272 --> 01:01:09.709
And you've been in back
the whole time?

1480
01:01:10.579 --> 01:01:12.973
Next subject, please.

1481
01:01:13.017 --> 01:01:14.845
Why would you do this?

1482
01:01:15.715 --> 01:01:17.108
[German accent]:
So sorry.

1483
01:01:17.151 --> 01:01:20.589
Uh, it was the only way to save
our beautiful yodeling.

1484
01:01:20.633 --> 01:01:22.069
Hickory.

1485
01:01:22.113 --> 01:01:24.419
But trust me, you need to get
out of here right away.

1486
01:01:24.463 --> 01:01:25.725
What are you doing, Hickory?

1487
01:01:25.769 --> 01:01:27.074
-Nein! -Dickory.
-[grunts]

1488
01:01:27.118 --> 01:01:28.075
Shut your mouth-hole, please!

1489
01:01:28.119 --> 01:01:29.903
-Let go!
-[grunting]

1490
01:01:29.947 --> 01:01:31.688
-We must save yodeling!
-Stop it! -Got you!

1491
01:01:31.731 --> 01:01:33.951
-[shouts]
-[laughs]

1492
01:01:33.994 --> 01:01:37.389
-I thought I heard a yodel.
-[gasps] Queen Barb.

1493
01:01:38.607 --> 01:01:40.827
-[pop riff plays]
-[Poppy gasps]

1494
01:01:40.871 --> 01:01:42.611
The final notes of Pop.

1495
01:01:42.655 --> 01:01:45.571
It will never invade
anyone's brain again.

1496
01:01:45.614 --> 01:01:47.704
I'm not gonna let you do this!

1497
01:01:52.839 --> 01:01:55.102
This is who I've been
worried about?

1498
01:01:55.146 --> 01:01:56.930
This little pipsqueak?

1499
01:01:56.974 --> 01:01:59.803
I'll never stop fighting
until I make things right.

1500
01:01:59.846 --> 01:02:01.805
-And I'm not a pipsqueak!
-Uh, yeah, you are,

1501
01:02:01.848 --> 01:02:03.763
'cause I'm, like, a whole
centimeter taller than you.

1502
01:02:03.807 --> 01:02:05.547
No! [grunts]
Leave me alone!

1503
01:02:05.591 --> 01:02:07.724
Leave you alone?
Uh, I'm sorry.

1504
01:02:07.767 --> 01:02:10.291
You were the one who was all
desperate to be best friends.

1505
01:02:10.335 --> 01:02:12.380
Get your hands off me.

1506
01:02:12.424 --> 01:02:13.555
Oh, okay. All right.

1507
01:02:13.599 --> 01:02:15.122
You're feisty.
I respect that.

1508
01:02:15.166 --> 01:02:17.429
Strong woman to strong woman,
am I right?

1509
01:02:17.472 --> 01:02:19.561
But you know
who else was feisty?

1510
01:02:20.780 --> 01:02:22.739
Pop Village.

1511
01:02:22.782 --> 01:02:24.175
[gasps]

1512
01:02:24.218 --> 01:02:26.090
Oh, no. No!

1513
01:02:27.134 --> 01:02:29.354
[panting]

1514
01:02:30.355 --> 01:02:31.922
Everyone! Everyone!

1515
01:02:31.965 --> 01:02:33.227
We're back!

1516
01:02:33.271 --> 01:02:34.489
[gasps]

1517
01:02:35.360 --> 01:02:37.754
[gasps] Oh, no.

1518
01:02:40.844 --> 01:02:42.802
-Biggie! You won't believe it!
-Hello, Biggie.

1519
01:02:42.846 --> 01:02:45.805
We were attacked
by Barb and her barbarians!

1520
01:02:45.849 --> 01:02:48.199
She took everybody
to Volcano Rock City.

1521
01:02:48.242 --> 01:02:49.548
It was scary.

1522
01:02:49.591 --> 01:02:50.810
Rock me, Daddy.

1523
01:02:50.854 --> 01:02:52.377
Mm, that's nice.

1524
01:02:54.205 --> 01:02:56.773
♪

1525
01:02:58.731 --> 01:03:01.516
I shouldn't have left her.

1526
01:03:01.560 --> 01:03:03.301
She wouldn't have left me.

1527
01:03:03.344 --> 01:03:05.651
Never, no matter
how scared she was.

1528
01:03:06.565 --> 01:03:09.350
I've got to go back.

1529
01:03:09.394 --> 01:03:11.918
We're coming with you, Biggie.

1530
01:03:11.962 --> 01:03:14.529
We got to go save
our best friend.

1531
01:03:14.573 --> 01:03:17.532
But how? We'll never
make it past security.

1532
01:03:17.576 --> 01:03:19.839
We'll overpower them
with muscles!

1533
01:03:19.883 --> 01:03:21.972
-[strains]
-[muscles squeak]

1534
01:03:23.538 --> 01:03:26.324
Or... we could overpower them

1535
01:03:26.367 --> 01:03:28.152
-with fashion.
-With fashion.

1536
01:03:28.195 --> 01:03:30.589
♪

1537
01:03:34.898 --> 01:03:36.377
Ouch.

1538
01:03:36.421 --> 01:03:37.596
[whimpers]:
Oh.

1539
01:03:39.206 --> 01:03:40.555
Ooh.

1540
01:03:40.599 --> 01:03:42.383
[rock music playing]

1541
01:03:42.427 --> 01:03:45.909
Rock and roll! [laughs]

1542
01:03:57.311 --> 01:03:59.531
[crowd cheering]

1543
01:04:00.924 --> 01:04:02.751
TROLL: All right,
where do we put these things?

1544
01:04:02.795 --> 01:04:04.318
TROLL 2:
I need a circuit hookup.

1545
01:04:04.362 --> 01:04:06.712
[quietly]: Okay, come on.
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

1546
01:04:06.755 --> 01:04:10.107
[bells jingling quietly]

1547
01:04:11.412 --> 01:04:13.893
Hey. Stop right there.

1548
01:04:13.937 --> 01:04:15.286
[jingling stops]

1549
01:04:15.329 --> 01:04:17.114
BIGGIE: Legsly, I told you
not to wear your anklet.

1550
01:04:17.157 --> 01:04:20.073
Only Rock Trolls
are allowed back here.

1551
01:04:20.117 --> 01:04:23.816
Well, it's funny
you should mention that,

1552
01:04:23.860 --> 01:04:28.690
because we are genuine
Hard Rockers.

1553
01:04:28.734 --> 01:04:30.997
[electric guitar strums weakly]

1554
01:04:32.042 --> 01:04:33.478
[deep voice]:
One, two, three, four!

1555
01:04:33.521 --> 01:04:34.914
-♪ Rainbows, unicorns
-[heavy metal music playing]

1556
01:04:34.958 --> 01:04:36.611
♪ Everything nice, yeah

1557
01:04:36.655 --> 01:04:38.265
♪ Sugarplums, fairy dust

1558
01:04:38.309 --> 01:04:40.964
♪ Everything nice, yeah

1559
01:04:41.007 --> 01:04:43.488
-♪ Brush your teeth.
-[hat squeaks]

1560
01:04:44.881 --> 01:04:46.012
Cool.

1561
01:04:46.056 --> 01:04:48.406
Hurry up.
The show's about to start, man.

1562
01:04:48.449 --> 01:04:50.147
Queen Barb's
about to go onstage.

1563
01:04:52.323 --> 01:04:53.585
We're screwed.

1564
01:04:53.628 --> 01:04:55.848
-[rock music playing]
-[crowd cheering]

1565
01:04:58.111 --> 01:04:59.591
BARB:
So, Popcorn,

1566
01:04:59.634 --> 01:05:01.158
is being my best friend

1567
01:05:01.201 --> 01:05:03.073
everything you could have
ever dreamed of?

1568
01:05:03.116 --> 01:05:05.292
-[grunts]
-[Barb and Trolls laugh]

1569
01:05:05.336 --> 01:05:06.903
I am not your best friend.

1570
01:05:06.946 --> 01:05:09.688
You don't have to be
embarrassed. I get it.

1571
01:05:09.731 --> 01:05:12.125
Being queen
can be kind of lonely.

1572
01:05:12.169 --> 01:05:14.649
CROWD [chanting]:
Barb! Barb! Barb! Barb! Barb!

1573
01:05:14.693 --> 01:05:17.043
[chanting fades]

1574
01:05:17.087 --> 01:05:20.220
There's all this pressure
to be a great queen.

1575
01:05:22.222 --> 01:05:24.703
And instead of real friends,
you're just surrounded by

1576
01:05:24.746 --> 01:05:28.098
people who just tell you
what you want to hear.

1577
01:05:29.360 --> 01:05:31.797
You know, other than
your terrible taste in music

1578
01:05:31.840 --> 01:05:34.495
and clothing
and general lifestyle,

1579
01:05:34.539 --> 01:05:36.889
you and me are the same,
Popsqueak.

1580
01:05:36.933 --> 01:05:38.282
Uh... [scoffs]
No, we're not.

1581
01:05:38.325 --> 01:05:40.849
We're both queens who just
want to unite the world.

1582
01:05:40.893 --> 01:05:42.503
You don't want
to unite the world.

1583
01:05:42.547 --> 01:05:44.027
You want to destroy it!

1584
01:05:44.070 --> 01:05:45.506
Nuh-uh. No way.

1585
01:05:45.550 --> 01:05:47.726
No. I don't know
who told you that.

1586
01:05:47.769 --> 01:05:50.859
Music has done nothing
but divide us.

1587
01:05:50.903 --> 01:05:52.992
Now that I have
the final string,

1588
01:05:53.036 --> 01:05:57.214
I can make us all one nation
of Trolls, under rock.

1589
01:05:57.257 --> 01:05:58.867
[guitar roars]

1590
01:05:58.911 --> 01:06:01.044
[magic jingling, whooshing]

1591
01:06:03.524 --> 01:06:05.135
[pop riff plays]

1592
01:06:12.229 --> 01:06:14.361
[rock riff echoes]

1593
01:06:14.405 --> 01:06:15.536
[laughs]

1594
01:06:15.580 --> 01:06:16.973
What are you gonna do?

1595
01:06:17.016 --> 01:06:19.584
Play the ultimate power chord,
and then...

1596
01:06:19.627 --> 01:06:20.759
[chuckles]

1597
01:06:20.802 --> 01:06:22.587
You'll see!

1598
01:06:26.808 --> 01:06:28.810
-["Barracuda" playing]
-[crowd cheering]

1599
01:06:33.990 --> 01:06:36.949
[crowd grunting in unison
to rhythm]

1600
01:06:36.993 --> 01:06:40.039
-♪ Queen Barb!
-[crowd cheering]

1601
01:06:40.083 --> 01:06:42.041
♪ So this ain't the end

1602
01:06:42.085 --> 01:06:46.480
♪ I saw you again today

1603
01:06:46.524 --> 01:06:49.657
♪ I had to turn my heart away

1604
01:06:49.701 --> 01:06:51.616
[crowd grunting in unison
to rhythm]

1605
01:06:51.659 --> 01:06:53.618
♪ Smile like the sun

1606
01:06:53.661 --> 01:06:57.926
♪ Kisses for everyone

1607
01:06:57.970 --> 01:07:00.755
♪ And tales, it never fails

1608
01:07:00.799 --> 01:07:02.409
[crowd grunting in unison
to rhythm]

1609
01:07:02.453 --> 01:07:06.065
♪ You're lying so low
in the weeds ♪

1610
01:07:06.109 --> 01:07:09.068
-♪ I bet you gonna ambush me
-Rock on!

1611
01:07:09.112 --> 01:07:10.243
Rock on!

1612
01:07:10.287 --> 01:07:12.898
♪ You'd have me
down, down, down, down ♪

1613
01:07:12.941 --> 01:07:14.813
♪ Down on my knees

1614
01:07:14.856 --> 01:07:17.294
♪ Now, won't ya?

1615
01:07:17.337 --> 01:07:19.209
[music and cheering stop]

1616
01:07:20.949 --> 01:07:24.083
♪ Barracuda!

1617
01:07:24.127 --> 01:07:26.085
-[music resumes]
-[crowd cheering]

1618
01:07:26.129 --> 01:07:28.000
[laughs] Bam!

1619
01:07:29.828 --> 01:07:32.091
-[playing note rhythmically]
-Hey! Look, Daddy!

1620
01:07:32.135 --> 01:07:34.050
I'm a rock star!

1621
01:07:34.093 --> 01:07:37.531
Uh, this is a little hot.

1622
01:07:37.575 --> 01:07:39.620
[chuckles]

1623
01:07:39.664 --> 01:07:40.621
[crowd cheering]

1624
01:07:40.665 --> 01:07:43.842
[electricity booming]

1625
01:07:47.019 --> 01:07:48.499
[crowd cheering, whooping]

1626
01:07:48.542 --> 01:07:50.631
Give it up
for your former leaders.

1627
01:07:50.675 --> 01:07:54.766
Funk, Country,
Techno, Classical...

1628
01:07:54.809 --> 01:07:56.463
[crowd booing]

1629
01:07:56.507 --> 01:07:58.987
...and worst of all, Pop.

1630
01:07:59.031 --> 01:08:00.337
[booing continues]

1631
01:08:04.254 --> 01:08:05.994
[electrical crackling,
whooshing]

1632
01:08:06.038 --> 01:08:09.911
Who wants to see what the
ultimate power chord can do?

1633
01:08:09.955 --> 01:08:11.870
[crowd cheering, whooping]

1634
01:08:14.307 --> 01:08:15.482
No. No!

1635
01:08:15.526 --> 01:08:16.875
[playing rock riff]

1636
01:08:16.918 --> 01:08:19.095
[chuckles, grunts]

1637
01:08:20.357 --> 01:08:21.880
[grunts]

1638
01:08:25.188 --> 01:08:26.841
[Sheila B whoops]

1639
01:08:26.885 --> 01:08:29.844
Ha! I guess a giant
comprehensive manual

1640
01:08:29.888 --> 01:08:31.585
does come in handy.

1641
01:08:31.629 --> 01:08:33.631
Bla-dow! Just in time!

1642
01:08:33.674 --> 01:08:34.632
Branch!

1643
01:08:34.675 --> 01:08:36.112
Well, isn't that puke.

1644
01:08:36.155 --> 01:08:39.245
Poppy's little boyfriend
came to crash the concert.

1645
01:08:39.289 --> 01:08:41.029
Too late, Branch.

1646
01:08:41.073 --> 01:08:42.292
Wait!

1647
01:08:49.386 --> 01:08:50.387
Branch!

1648
01:08:55.087 --> 01:08:56.610
[crowd murmuring quietly]

1649
01:08:56.654 --> 01:08:58.046
No.

1650
01:09:03.487 --> 01:09:05.489
[crackling]

1651
01:09:08.753 --> 01:09:10.233
Branch.

1652
01:09:12.583 --> 01:09:14.498
Rock on!

1653
01:09:14.541 --> 01:09:16.326
[crowd cheering]

1654
01:09:16.369 --> 01:09:18.806
Oh, sick! Totally works.

1655
01:09:18.850 --> 01:09:20.808
Who's ready to get
rippin' tattoos

1656
01:09:20.852 --> 01:09:24.203
everywhere but our faces in
case we still need office jobs?

1657
01:09:24.247 --> 01:09:25.422
Rah!

1658
01:09:25.465 --> 01:09:27.946
You're turning everyone
into rock zombies?

1659
01:09:27.989 --> 01:09:31.079
Yep. I can't wait
to party with you, Poppy.

1660
01:09:31.123 --> 01:09:34.344
[rock music playing]

1661
01:09:53.189 --> 01:09:55.191
-[grunts]
-Rock and roll!

1662
01:09:56.366 --> 01:09:57.932
Dude.

1663
01:09:57.976 --> 01:09:59.064
[door creaks]

1664
01:09:59.107 --> 01:10:01.109
BARB:
Not so fast, Popsqueak.

1665
01:10:01.153 --> 01:10:03.938
Hey, boy toy, it's mullet time.

1666
01:10:03.982 --> 01:10:07.290
[strains, growls]

1667
01:10:09.248 --> 01:10:10.423
[grunts]

1668
01:10:10.467 --> 01:10:11.816
[playing rock riff]

1669
01:10:15.167 --> 01:10:16.212
[grunts]

1670
01:10:21.652 --> 01:10:24.959
♪

1671
01:10:25.003 --> 01:10:27.527
-[gasps]
-[gasps]

1672
01:10:27.571 --> 01:10:30.487
Who wants to party?!

1673
01:10:30.530 --> 01:10:32.010
Without smiling.

1674
01:10:32.053 --> 01:10:34.273
[crowd cheering]

1675
01:10:34.317 --> 01:10:36.101
Finish them off.

1676
01:10:38.234 --> 01:10:40.105
-[gasps]
-[rock riff playing]

1677
01:10:54.554 --> 01:10:55.816
What are you doing?

1678
01:10:55.860 --> 01:10:58.602
You're supposed to be
a rock zombie!

1679
01:10:58.645 --> 01:11:00.299
Gumdrops.

1680
01:11:00.343 --> 01:11:01.822
Soundproof and delicious.

1681
01:11:01.866 --> 01:11:03.346
-[gulps]
-[Trolls groaning in disgust]

1682
01:11:03.389 --> 01:11:05.478
[Southern accent]: She learned
that from watching me.

1683
01:11:05.522 --> 01:11:06.784
Give me that!

1684
01:11:06.827 --> 01:11:08.525
I'm not gonna let you
do this to anyone else!

1685
01:11:08.568 --> 01:11:11.876
A world where everyone looks
the same and sounds the same?

1686
01:11:11.919 --> 01:11:13.921
That's not harmony.

1687
01:11:13.965 --> 01:11:15.358
RIFF:
Hey, Barb?

1688
01:11:16.359 --> 01:11:17.316
Hi.

1689
01:11:17.360 --> 01:11:19.231
Maybe Queen Poppy has a point.

1690
01:11:19.275 --> 01:11:22.452
If we all look the same,
act the same, dress the same,

1691
01:11:22.495 --> 01:11:26.151
how will anyone know
we're cool or something?

1692
01:11:26.194 --> 01:11:28.414
-[crowd murmuring]
-TROLL: Yeah. He's got a point.

1693
01:11:28.458 --> 01:11:30.111
A good point.

1694
01:11:30.155 --> 01:11:33.332
A good queen listens.

1695
01:11:35.552 --> 01:11:38.511
Real harmony
takes lots of voices.

1696
01:11:38.555 --> 01:11:39.556
[grunts]

1697
01:11:39.599 --> 01:11:41.340
Different voices!

1698
01:11:41.384 --> 01:11:43.516
[loud whooshing]

1699
01:11:43.560 --> 01:11:46.345
[loud musical rumbling]

1700
01:11:50.523 --> 01:11:52.090
[rumbling stops]

1701
01:11:57.922 --> 01:11:59.793
POPPY [quietly]:
Oh.

1702
01:11:59.837 --> 01:12:01.055
[Branch grunts]

1703
01:12:04.929 --> 01:12:07.453
Branch!

1704
01:12:07.497 --> 01:12:09.412
No.

1705
01:12:09.455 --> 01:12:11.979
[quiet electrical jingling
and whooshing]

1706
01:12:14.460 --> 01:12:16.201
My strings.

1707
01:12:19.073 --> 01:12:21.859
[panting]

1708
01:12:21.902 --> 01:12:23.643
What have you done?

1709
01:12:23.687 --> 01:12:26.254
You've destroyed music!

1710
01:12:26.298 --> 01:12:28.431
-[crowd gasping, murmuring]
-Give it up, everybody.

1711
01:12:28.474 --> 01:12:33.697
Thanks to the Queen of Pop,
we've all lost our music.

1712
01:12:35.568 --> 01:12:38.005
History repeats itself.

1713
01:12:38.049 --> 01:12:41.487
Pop has ruined everything.

1714
01:12:56.807 --> 01:13:00.027
[heartbeat thumping faintly]

1715
01:13:12.170 --> 01:13:15.391
[heartbeat thumping
rhythmically over speakers]

1716
01:13:21.222 --> 01:13:23.399
-[crowd murmuring quietly]
-[rhythmic heartbeat continues]

1717
01:13:30.667 --> 01:13:32.669
[beatboxing to rhythm]

1718
01:13:38.501 --> 01:13:40.938
Those are my sons.

1719
01:13:40.981 --> 01:13:42.505
Making music.

1720
01:13:42.548 --> 01:13:46.378
[heartbeat and beatboxing
continue]

1721
01:13:49.381 --> 01:13:51.557
[clapping and tapping
to rhythm]

1722
01:13:53.820 --> 01:13:57.215
[crowd clapping and stomping
to rhythm, excited chatter]

1723
01:14:07.268 --> 01:14:09.009
-[music stops]
-[heartbeat continues]

1724
01:14:09.053 --> 01:14:12.448
Queen Barb can't take away
something that is inside us.

1725
01:14:13.710 --> 01:14:16.539
Because that's where music
really comes from.

1726
01:14:18.279 --> 01:14:22.022
It started with the strings,
but now it comes from us.

1727
01:14:22.066 --> 01:14:24.242
[Trolls vocalizing melodically]

1728
01:14:29.987 --> 01:14:33.077
Yeah, it comes from
our experiences.

1729
01:14:33.120 --> 01:14:34.600
Our lives.

1730
01:14:34.644 --> 01:14:36.123
Our culture.

1731
01:14:36.167 --> 01:14:37.647
[melodic vocalizing continues]

1732
01:14:37.690 --> 01:14:39.692
Beautiful. [laughs]

1733
01:14:39.736 --> 01:14:41.302
Listen to that.

1734
01:14:41.346 --> 01:14:43.522
Barb can't take that away.

1735
01:14:43.566 --> 01:14:45.742
[melodic vocalizing continues]

1736
01:15:06.980 --> 01:15:09.200
[vocalizing stops]

1737
01:15:09.983 --> 01:15:14.248
♪ Let me hear you sing

1738
01:15:16.773 --> 01:15:19.906
♪ Sing it together

1739
01:15:19.950 --> 01:15:22.779
♪ Louder than ever

1740
01:15:24.781 --> 01:15:26.696
♪ Forget everything

1741
01:15:26.739 --> 01:15:28.741
POPPY and BRANCH [harmonizing]:
♪ Just sing

1742
01:15:28.785 --> 01:15:32.223
♪ Like it's
what we've been missing ♪

1743
01:15:32.266 --> 01:15:36.967
♪ And they're gonna
listen, listen ♪

1744
01:15:37.010 --> 01:15:39.273
♪ Forget everything

1745
01:15:39.317 --> 01:15:43.103
-♪ Just sing
-[magic chiming]

1746
01:15:43.147 --> 01:15:44.583
Dad?

1747
01:15:44.627 --> 01:15:46.585
-It's all right, Barbara.
-[playing melody]

1748
01:15:46.629 --> 01:15:49.457
Just let everyone be
what they want to be.

1749
01:15:49.501 --> 01:15:51.721
-Including you.
-[growling softly]

1750
01:15:53.505 --> 01:15:54.593
[Trolls humming along]

1751
01:15:54.637 --> 01:15:57.204
♪ You think
you've gotta hide it ♪

1752
01:15:59.163 --> 01:16:02.122
♪ Don't keep it on the shelf

1753
01:16:02.166 --> 01:16:04.603
♪ Let your waist start moving

1754
01:16:04.647 --> 01:16:07.737
♪ Watch the way
I do it, do it ♪

1755
01:16:07.780 --> 01:16:12.480
♪ See me do it
like nobody else ♪

1756
01:16:12.524 --> 01:16:15.005
♪ If we sing it all together

1757
01:16:15.048 --> 01:16:17.181
♪ If we sing it all as one

1758
01:16:17.224 --> 01:16:19.444
♪ It's louder than yourself

1759
01:16:19.487 --> 01:16:20.880
♪ All together, everyone

1760
01:16:20.924 --> 01:16:22.926
-♪ Everybody's looking
-♪ Sing it loud now

1761
01:16:22.969 --> 01:16:24.362
♪ Watch the way we do it

1762
01:16:24.405 --> 01:16:25.624
-♪ Hold up, watch out
how I do it ♪ - Do it ♪

1763
01:16:25.668 --> 01:16:28.366
♪ 'Cause we do it
like nobody else ♪

1764
01:16:28.409 --> 01:16:30.368
♪ Let me hear you sing

1765
01:16:30.411 --> 01:16:33.284
♪ Don't you stop it,
don't you fight it ♪

1766
